{"content":[{"c":["MESHULLAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Forefather of Shaphan, the royal secretary to King Josiah of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.3","r":"2Kgs.22.3","rawR":"2Kgs.22.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.3","value":"2Kgs.22.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Zerubbabel’s son and a descendant of David (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.19","r":"1Chr.3.19","rawR":"1Chr.3.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.19","value":"1Chr.3.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:19"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Gadite leader registered during the reigns of Jotham, king of Judah (950–932 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), and Jeroboam II, king of Israel (993–953 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.13","r":"1Chr.5.13","rawR":"1Chr.5.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.13","value":"1Chr.5.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Benjamite and a descendant of Elpaal (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.17","r":"1Chr.8.17","rawR":"1Chr.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.17","value":"1Chr.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Benjamite and the father of Sallu, a resident in Jerusalem during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.7","r":"1Chr.9.7","rawR":"1Chr.9.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.7","value":"1Chr.9.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.7","r":"Neh.11.7","rawR":"Neh.11.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.7","value":"Neh.11.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Benjamite and the son of Shephatiah, who resided in Jerusalem during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.8","r":"1Chr.9.8","rawR":"1Chr.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.8","value":"1Chr.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Priest, the son of Zadok and the father of Hilkiah, whose descendants served in Jerusalem’s sanctuary during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","r":"1Chr.9.11","rawR":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.11","value":"1Chr.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.11","r":"Neh.11.11","rawR":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.11","value":"Neh.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:11"},"). He is probably identical with Shallum in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.12-13","r":"1Chr.6.12-13","rawR":"1Chr.6.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.12-13","value":"1Chr.6.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:12-13"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Priest, the son of Meshillemith and a forefather of Adaiah. Adaiah served in Jerusalem’s sanctuary during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.12","r":"1Chr.9.12","rawR":"1Chr.9.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.12","value":"1Chr.9.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Kohathite Levite who was appointed to oversee the repair of the temple during King Josiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.12","r":"2Chr.34.12","rawR":"2Chr.34.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.12","value":"2Chr.34.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the Jewish leaders whom Ezra sent to Iddo at Casiphia to gather Levites and temple servants for the caravan of Jews returning to Palestine from Babylonia (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.16","r":"Ezra.8.16","rawR":"Ezra.8.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.16","value":"Ezra.8.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. One who opposed Ezra’s suggestion that the sons of Israel should divorce the foreign women they had married since returning to Palestine from exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.15","r":"Ezra.10.15","rawR":"Ezra.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.15","value":"Ezra.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. Bani’s son, who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.29","r":"Ezra.10.29","rawR":"Ezra.10.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.29","value":"Ezra.10.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["13. Berekiah’s son, who rebuilt a section of the Jerusalem wall during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.4,30","r":"Neh.3.4,30","rawR":"Neh.3.4,30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.4,30","value":"Neh.3.4,30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:4, 30"},"). His daughter married Jehohanan, the son of Tobiah the Ammonite (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.6.18","r":"Neh.6.18","rawR":"Neh.6.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.6.18","value":"Neh.6.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["14. Besodeiah’s son, who with Joiada repaired the Old Gate in the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.6","r":"Neh.3.6","rawR":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.6","value":"Neh.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["15. One of the men who stood to Ezra’s left when Ezra read the law to the people (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.8.4","r":"Neh.8.4","rawR":"Neh.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.8.4","value":"Neh.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 8:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["16. One of the priests who set his seal on the covenant of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.7","r":"Neh.10.7","rawR":"Neh.10.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.7","value":"Neh.10.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["17. One of the leaders of Israel who set his seal on the covenant of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.20","r":"Neh.10.20","rawR":"Neh.10.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.20","value":"Neh.10.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["18. Head of Ezra’s priestly family during the days of Joiakim, the high priest, in postexilic Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.13","r":"Neh.12.13","rawR":"Neh.12.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.13","value":"Neh.12.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["19. Head of Ginnethon’s priestly family during the days of Joiakim (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.16","r":"Neh.12.16","rawR":"Neh.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.16","value":"Neh.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["20. One of the gatekeepers during the days of the high priest Joiakim (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.25","r":"Neh.12.25","rawR":"Neh.12.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.25","value":"Neh.12.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:25"},"); perhaps identifiable with Shallum in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.17","r":"1Chr.9.17","rawR":"1Chr.9.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.17","value":"1Chr.9.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 9:17"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["21. One of the princes of Judah who participated in the dedication of the Jerusalem wall during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.33","r":"Neh.12.33","rawR":"Neh.12.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.33","value":"Neh.12.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Meshullam","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 22:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.22.3","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.22.3","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.22.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstre